      "problem": "$\\frac{1}{3}(3x-9y+27)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the distributive law and simplifying, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}(3x-9y+27) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9y+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 27 & = \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3}-\\frac{9y}{3}+\\frac{27}{3} & = \\\\ x-3y+9\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
